		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4537&amp;p=33810#p33810"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Here another proposal from a  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_rolleyes.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":roll:" title="Rolling Eyes"> bloody beginner:<br><br>When I added a channel for my home repeater I put its DMR-ID in that field. But this is wrong. <br><br>Maybe there is space enough in that window to write a remark like „leave blank for repeaters“. <br>But how is this for hotspots? If it’s the same it should be: <br><img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_arrow.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":arrow:" title="Arrow">  „leave blank for repeaters or hotspots“.<br><br>Thanks for consider this VK3KYY</div></blockquote>DMR ID in the channel setup in  CPS is only used if you want to be identified by some other DMR ID for a specific channel.<br>Normally it's the DMR ID that you set under "DMR ID and Callsign" that is used as your own DMR ID.<br>It should never be the repeaters ID in that field, and it's normally blank for a hotspot channel too (unless you pretend to be someone else).<br><br>There are some help texts defined but not for that field ( Enable HelpView )<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Wed Oct 30, 2024 6:53 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
